From 041965d9150a99cbda1ddf46552ee195fce8233e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 18 May 2026 09:16:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] armchina-npu: force ACPI D0 when all NPU pd_core[] NULL (BIOS
 v1.0)

On BIOS v1.0, CRE0/CRE1/CRE2 NPU core devices lack _HID in the DSDT.
bus_find_device_by_fwnode() returns NULL for all three cores. After the
fwnode child loop, all pd_core[] entries are NULL, so pm_runtime_resume_and_get
is skipped entirely.

Without explicit D0 activation, ACPI puts CIXH4000 in D3cold during
device scan (because _PR0 power transition via SCMI fails in BIOS v1.0).
armchina_aipu_probe() then reads the version register on unpowered
hardware and gets garbage (value 5) -> EINVAL.

Fix: when all pd_core[] are NULL, call acpi_device_set_power(D0) before
armchina_aipu_probe(). This forces the ACPI _PS0 path (bypassing the
_PR0/SCMI path) to bring hardware to D0 regardless of power domain
availability.
---
 drivers/misc/armchina-npu/sky1/sky1.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/misc/armchina-npu/sky1/sky1.c b/drivers/misc/armchina-npu/sky1/sky1.c
index eef3b621c26c..d09f3ab7d9b6 100644
--- a/drivers/misc/armchina-npu/sky1/sky1.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/armchina-npu/sky1/sky1.c
@@ -428,6 +428,19 @@ static int sky1_npu_probe(struct platform_device *p_dev)
 			if (ret < 0)
 				goto npu_probe_failed;
 		}
+		/* If all pd_core[] are NULL (BIOS v1.0 missing _HID on CRE devices),
+		 * force D0 via ACPI to ensure hardware is powered before probing. */
+		{
+			int all_null = 1;
+			for (i = 0; i < CIX_NPU_PD_NUM; i++)
+				if (sky1_npu_pd_core_valid(cix_aipu_priv->pd_core[i]))
+					{ all_null = 0; break; }
+			if (all_null) {
+				struct acpi_device *adev = ACPI_COMPANION(&p_dev->dev);
+				if (adev)
+					acpi_device_set_power(adev, ACPI_STATE_D0);
+			}
+		}
     }
 
     ret = armchina_aipu_probe(p_dev, &sky1, &sky1_ops);
-- 
